WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.840
We're going to talk about libraries and modules.

00:03.840 --> 00:06.600
So I've been using a few modules here and there.

00:06.600 --> 00:10.560
You've seen me import a few things, date time, random.

00:10.560 --> 00:13.600
There was a library that helped me do a live reloading

00:13.600 --> 00:15.800
of my modules.

00:15.800 --> 00:17.600
And that's just the thing about Python.

00:17.600 --> 00:20.360
The language was designed to be batteries included.

00:20.360 --> 00:26.240
It has a rich and versatile standard library, which

00:26.240 --> 00:27.840
is immediately available.

00:27.840 --> 00:30.400
I didn't have to download or install anything external.

00:30.400 --> 00:32.720
It just comes with the interpreter.

00:32.720 --> 00:36.080
And many people believe that this

00:36.080 --> 00:39.720
has given the Python language a head start in a lot of cases.

00:42.720 --> 00:47.280
It's really helped vault Python to be the popular tool

00:47.280 --> 00:49.760
that it is today.

00:49.760 --> 00:53.000
So let's take a look at some of those helpful packages

00:53.000 --> 00:55.200
in the standard library.

00:55.200 --> 00:59.400
One of the downsides of the standard library

00:59.400 --> 01:08.440
is that it's really optimized for having a rich feature

01:08.440 --> 01:08.920
set.

01:08.920 --> 01:11.400
And it's also optimized for backwards compatibility.

01:11.400 --> 01:16.720
So as the library has the Python language grows.

01:16.720 --> 01:18.400
For the most part, they try to maintain

01:18.400 --> 01:22.040
as much backwards compatibility as possible.

01:22.040 --> 01:24.080
That means that some of the included libraries

01:24.080 --> 01:25.400
are a little bit hard to use.

01:25.400 --> 01:30.200
But it's really easy to install external libraries as well.

01:30.200 --> 01:37.520
Some of the commonly used features of the standard library

01:37.520 --> 01:41.200
sits, S-Y-S, the provide system specific parameters

01:41.200 --> 01:43.040
and functions.

01:43.040 --> 01:47.360
OS has a lot of methods available for working

01:47.360 --> 01:49.960
with the operating system interface.

01:49.960 --> 01:52.960
And there's a great OS path submodule that

01:52.960 --> 01:58.120
helps us handle files on the file path.

01:58.120 --> 02:01.840
Math gives us a lot of advanced math functions

02:01.840 --> 02:04.240
and JSON.

02:04.240 --> 02:10.000
Helps us as an easy-to-use JSON parser and encoder.

02:10.000 --> 02:12.960
Python even gives you a lot of other built-in libraries,

02:12.960 --> 02:18.280
like database access, logging, internet protocols, multimedia.

02:18.280 --> 02:20.400
There's a debugger.

02:20.400 --> 02:24.200
And there are libraries for extending Python itself.

